From 6c282ad70b5a0f3cc2f93f16dabaa872a7c72abd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 09:15:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] bsc.cabal: carve the library into four sublibraries

Establish the component structure of doc/engine-first-plan.md section 2 on
the B0 manifest: private sublibraries bsc-common, bsc-semantic, bsc-verilog
and bsc-bluesim, with the public bsc library becoming a facade that
re-exports every module, so executables, testsuite stanzas and external
consumers are unchanged.

The partition is derived from the module import graph at this revision,
not assigned by hand: a module reachable from exactly one producer's entry
modules belongs to that producer; anything shared by two producers, or by
a producer and the semantic pipeline, sinks to bsc-common; FFI- and
C-source-backed modules (HTcl, STP/STPFFI, Yices/YicesFFI, FSTRead) and
the generated modules (BuildSystem, BuildVersion, Warmup) are pinned to
bsc-common, which also carries the c-sources, include-dirs and
extra-libraries. Result: bsc-common 143 modules, bsc-semantic 71,
bsc-verilog 14, bsc-bluesim 22; no module needs to import across producer
boundaries, so the component DAG is common <- {semantic, verilog, bluesim}
<- facade with no residual glue modules.

SetupHooks retargets accordingly: the generated-module declaration and
rules and the Tcl link configuration move from the main library to
bsc-common; the solver rpath applies to both the facade (inherited by
executables) and bsc-common (whose dynamic object records the solver
dependencies).

Notes for review:
- Packaging-only change: no source file moves, no module renames, and the
  re-exported module set is byte-for-byte the previous exposed-modules
  list. VIOProps stays whole in bsc-verilog; its getIOPropsA/getIOProps
  split into semantic/verilog is the plan's later P3 step, as is moving
  driver stage orchestration out of app/bsc.hs (several shared passes,
  e.g. ASchedule, ITransform, GenABin, sit in bsc-common today because
  backends genuinely import them).
- Validated statically only (import-graph closure and component-DAG check
  over all 250 modules; zero violations). This environment has no GHC or
  cabal, so it awaits cabal build and the whole testsuite before adoption.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
